---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Leagues of Votann Beginner's Guide — Warhammer 40k"
  description="New to Leagues of Votann? Learn how the Kin play, which League to choose, how to paint their armor, and exactly what to buy first."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 pb-12 border-b border-[#2a2a35]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/factions/" class="text-sm text-[#4a4855] hover:text-[#8a8590] transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">
        ← All Factions
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-6">
        <div class="text-6xl">⛏️</div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#c9a84c] text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase mb-2 font-display">Faction Guide</p>
          <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Leagues of Votann</h1>
          <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            Space dwarves. Officially, they are the Kin — ancient human descendants who mine 
            the deep void beyond the Imperium's reach. Stocky, bearded, culturally obsessed 
            with grudges and trade. One of the most beginner-friendly shooting armies in 40k.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick stats -->
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Playstyle</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">Tough Shooting Dwarves</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Painting</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-400">Medium</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Rules</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-green-400">Easy–Medium</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Starter Cost</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">~$160</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-3 italic">*One of the more beginner-friendly factions in 40k. The game plan is simple; the execution is satisfying.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lore -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">Who are the Kin?</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg">
        <p>
          In the earliest days of humanity's expansion into the stars, before the Imperium existed, 
          before even the Age of Technology reached its peak, humans spread further than history 
          remembers. Some went so deep into the galactic core that even the vast records of the 
          Administratum lost track of them. The Leagues of Votann are their descendants.
        </p>
        <p>
          Officially, the Imperium calls them the Kin — acknowledging them cautiously as human, 
          but uneasy about what they've become. Unofficially, everyone calls them space dwarves. 
          They are stocky, compact, bearded, and culturally obsessed with two things: 
          trade and grudges. A debt paid is a foundation of civilization. A debt unpaid 
          is an affront that persists across generations. They keep literal records of grudges 
          — and they settle them.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each League is organized around an <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Ancestor Core</strong> — 
          a vast, ancient artificial intelligence that has accumulated thousands of years of 
          cultural memory, ancestral knowledge, and tactical expertise. The Kin consult these 
          AIs for guidance, upload their experiences to them upon death, and revere them as 
          something between a computer, a god, and a library. This is technically heresy under 
          Imperial law. The Imperium doesn't know. The Kin don't particularly care.
        </p>
        <p>
          They mine the deep void for rare resources the Imperium can barely reach — 
          exotic minerals, unstable elements, things that require traversing regions of 
          space so hostile that only their hardened Ironkin robots and heavily armored 
          Hearthkyn warriors can survive. They are not allied with the Imperium. 
          They are not enemies of the Imperium. They are simply out there, getting on with it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Playstyle -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">How they play on the table</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg mb-10">
        <p>
          Leagues of Votann are a <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">sturdy mid-range shooting army</strong> 
          with a simple, satisfying game plan: advance toward the midfield, shoot everything, 
          hold what you take. They are tougher than their point cost suggests and hit harder 
          at close-to-mid range than comparable armies. Not subtle. Devastatingly effective.
        </p>
        <p>
          The army's defining mechanic is <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Judgement tokens</strong>. 
          When your units target an enemy, that enemy can accumulate Judgement tokens. 
          Judged enemies are easier to wound — their toughness is effectively reduced 
          in your rolls. Against a Judged target, everything in your army performs better. 
          Smart play means choosing the right enemy to pile tokens on and then committing 
          your whole army to eliminating that target efficiently.
        </p>
        <p>
          The unit lineup is straightforward: 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Hearthkyn Warriors</strong> are your bread-and-butter troops — 
          dependable and tactically flexible. 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Einhyr Hearthguard</strong> are elite plasma-armed heavy infantry. 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Brôkhyr Thunderkyn</strong> are walking heavy weapons platforms. 
          The <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Einhyr Champion</strong> leads from the front, 
          a brutal melee character who can anchor a combat or duel characters.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-green-400">Votann are for you if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✓ You love the space dwarf aesthetic</li>
            <li>✓ You want a forgiving, beginner-friendly army</li>
            <li>✓ You enjoy sturdy, mid-range shooting</li>
            <li>✓ You want a relatively small model count</li>
            <li>✓ You like a clear game plan: advance and shoot</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-red-400">Maybe look elsewhere if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✗ You want a huge horde of cheap models</li>
            <li>✗ You want long-range artillery shooting</li>
            <li>✗ You want the deepest, most complex rules</li>
            <li>✗ You prefer melee-dominant armies</li>
            <li>✗ You want the most popular faction (Votann are rare)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- League choice -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">Choose your League</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        Each League has canonical color schemes, rules bonuses, and cultural identity. 
        Pick with your gut — you'll be painting these beards for a while.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        {[
          {
            name: 'Ymyr Conglomerate',
            colors: 'Dark grey / bronze',
            swatch: 'bg-slate-600',
            playstyle: 'Resilient and methodical',
            painting: 'Easy',
            paintColor: 'text-green-400',
            desc: 'The industrial miners. Dark grey armor with bronze trim gives a grim, utilitarian look that\'s very forgiving to paint. Popular starter choice — the grey and bronze palette suits a beginner\'s brush well.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Urani-Surtr Regulates',
            colors: 'Dark red / brass',
            swatch: 'bg-red-900',
            playstyle: 'Aggressive and punishing',
            painting: 'Easy–Medium',
            paintColor: 'text-green-400',
            desc: 'The fire-and-iron aesthetic. Deep red armor with brass detailing. A strong visual contrast that looks striking on the table and paints up quickly using shade-over-base techniques.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Trans-Hyperian Alliance',
            colors: 'Blue / gold',
            swatch: 'bg-blue-800',
            playstyle: 'Precision and trade',
            painting: 'Medium',
            paintColor: 'text-yellow-400',
            desc: 'The void traders and navigators. Bright blue armor with gold trim looks exceptional and is immediately recognizable. Slightly more effort to achieve clean blue panels, but the result is one of the best-looking Votann schemes.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Custom League',
            colors: 'Your choice',
            swatch: 'bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-800 to-teal-700',
            playstyle: 'Any',
            painting: 'Varies',
            paintColor: 'text-[#8a8590]',
            desc: 'The Votann have numerous Leagues beyond the canonical ones. You can invent your own colors and background. The models\' armor surfaces and clean lines suit almost any color scheme you choose.',
          },
        ].map(league => (
          <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
              <div class={`w-4 h-full min-h-[48px] rounded ${league.swatch} flex-shrink-0`}></div>
              <div class="flex-1">
                <div class="flex items-center flex-wrap gap-3 mb-1">
                  <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-lg">{league.name}</h3>
                  <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">{league.colors}</span>
                  <span class={`text-xs font-semibold ${league.paintColor}`}>Painting: {league.painting}</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-xs mb-2">Playstyle: {league.playstyle}</p>
                <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">{league.desc}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Painting -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">How to paint Leagues of Votann</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        Using Ymyr Conglomerate (grey / bronze) as the example — the most forgiving scheme 
        for beginners and fast to batch paint across a whole squad.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 mb-10">
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">1</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Prime grey, base coat armor Mechanicus Standard Grey</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Grey Seer spray primer, then Mechanicus Standard Grey over all armor panels. For Urani-Surtr: Khorne Red. For Trans-Hyperian: Kantor Blue. One pass with a large brush covers the flat surfaces fast.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">2</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Wash with Nuln Oil</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Apply Nuln Oil over all the armor. It pools in the deep recesses between equipment panels and creates instant depth. The grey armor now looks like something that's been through deep-void mining runs.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">3</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Drybrush raised panels Administratum Grey</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Light drybrush of Administratum Grey over the raised armor edges and surfaces. The Votann models have beautifully defined panel lines — drybrushing creates clean edge highlights automatically without careful brush control.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">4</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Bronze trim — Balthasar Gold then Agrax Earthshade</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Apply Balthasar Gold to all the bronze trim, equipment frames, and rune decorations. Wash with Agrax Earthshade to make it look aged and worked. This is the defining detail that makes the Ymyr scheme instantly recognizable.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">5</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Skin and beards</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Kislev Flesh on exposed skin, Reikland Fleshshade into recesses. Beards: Rakarth Flesh base → Agrax Earthshade → Pallid Wych Flesh highlight. The beards are small but very characterful — worth taking a little time.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">6</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Weapons and energy effects</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Weapon casings: Abaddon Black or Leadbelcher depending on the weapon type. Energy cells and plasma coils: Sotek Green or Aethermatic Blue Contrast for a distinctive sci-fi glow. Eye lenses: Moot Green with a white dot highlight.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-2">The Contrast paint shortcut</h3>
        <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Prime <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Wraithbone</strong> → apply 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Basilicanum Grey Contrast</strong> over armor → 
          pick out trim in Balthasar Gold and wash with Agrax → 
          apply <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Guilliman Flesh Contrast</strong> over skin. 
          The Contrast paints do all the shading automatically. 
          Surprisingly complete result for three colors and thirty minutes per model.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- What to buy -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">What to buy first</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-10 text-lg">Start with the Combat Patrol. Paint it before buying anything else — 19 models is a good first project.</p>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <span class="bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-display mr-2">Start Here</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$160</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Combat Patrol: Leagues of Votann</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Includes an Einhyr Champion (melee character), 3 Brôkhyr Thunderkyn (heavy weapons), 
          5 Einhyr Hearthguard (elite plasma infantry), and 10 Hearthkyn Warriors (core troops) — 
          19 models total. Every unit type in the core army, ready to learn the Judgement mechanic 
          and the advance-and-shoot game plan from day one.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0CW8DBGWM?tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Search Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-3">
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$60 · first expansion</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Hearthkyn Warriors (second squad)</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          A second Hearthkyn Warriors box gives you more bodies to hold objectives, 
          more wounds to absorb shooting, and the option to build variant weapon loadouts. 
          Votann armies want reliable troop presence and a second Warriors squad 
          delivers exactly that.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=hearthkyn+warriors+leagues+of+votann+warhammer&tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Search Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Paints -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-4">Paints you need (Ymyr Conglomerate)</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            { name: 'Grey Seer Spray', use: 'Primer — ideal for grey and contrast schemes', required: true },
            { name: 'Mechanicus Standard Grey', use: 'Armor base coat', required: true },
            { name: 'Nuln Oil', use: 'Shade wash — all armor and recesses', required: true },
            { name: 'Administratum Grey', use: 'Drybrush — raised armor panels', required: true },
            { name: 'Balthasar Gold', use: 'Bronze trim and equipment detail', required: true },
            { name: 'Agrax Earthshade', use: 'Shade for bronze areas and beards', required: true },
            { name: 'Kislev Flesh', use: 'Skin tone', required: true },
            { name: 'Reikland Fleshshade', use: 'Skin shade wash', required: true },
            { name: 'Aethermatic Blue', use: 'Energy cells and plasma glow effects', required: false },
          ].map(paint => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class={`text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 font-display ${paint.required ? 'bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113]' : 'border border-[#2a2a35] text-[#4a4855]'}`}>
                {paint.required ? 'Essential' : 'Optional'}
              </span>
              <div>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold">{paint.name}</span>
                <span class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm"> — {paint.use}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">Different League? Swap Mechanicus Standard Grey for your League's armor color. Everything else works the same.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Cost breakdown -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-8">Honest cost breakdown</h2>
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        {[
          { item: 'Combat Patrol: Leagues of Votann', cost: '~$160', note: '19 models — strong patrol force' },
          { item: 'Essential paints (8)', cost: '~$48', note: 'Grey armor + bronze + skin + shade' },
          { item: 'Basing supplies', cost: '~$12', note: 'Texture paint + tufts + drybrush color' },
          { item: 'Clippers + hobby knife', cost: '~$20', note: 'One-time purchase' },
          { item: 'Plastic glue', cost: '~$7', note: 'Sturdy infantry builds benefit from plastic glue' },
        ].map((row, i) => (
          <div class={`flex items-start justify-between px-5 py-4 gap-4 ${i % 2 === 0 ? '' : 'bg-[#111113]'}`}>
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold">{row.item}</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-0.5">{row.note}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] flex-shrink-0">{row.cost}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 bg-[#1f1d14] border-t border-[#c9a84c]">
          <p class="font-display font-semibold">All-in starter total</p>
          <span class="font-display font-bold text-[#c9a84c] text-lg">~$247</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">
        Votann are a relatively new faction (released 2022) so the model range is smaller than older armies. 
        The core kit selection is tightly designed — fewer units means fewer purchasing decisions, 
        which is actually a beginner advantage.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="px-6 py-20 text-center">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold mb-4">Hold the grudge. Settle the debt.</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg mb-8">
        Choose your League, grab the Combat Patrol, and advance into the midfield. 
        The Kin don't retreat. They don't negotiate from weakness. They advance, 
        they shoot, and they remember everything.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a
          href="/painting"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display tracking-wide"
        >
          Painting Guide →
        </a>
        <a
          href="/quiz"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Retake the Quiz
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
